      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The sweet smell could indeed be coming from chemicals added to the hydroponic solution, which are then released as a vapor. Activated carbon filters can effectively neutralize organic compounds, such as sugars and other chemicals. However, to target specific volatile organic compounds (VOCs) and synthetic additives, look for filters with technologies like Granular Activated Carbon (GAC) or Xenon-based filters. You may also consider using an air scrubber with built-in UV light, which can help break down and destroy odor-causing bacteria and microorganisms.",
